                (gate-verdict . pass)
                (gate-verdict-label . "resequenced green at implementation-sha (both contract suites exit 0 and the W2 SHA256SUMS verify OK); the PR squash-merge and post-merge gate confirmation are the runtime coordinator's owned flow and are not claimed as done inside this record")
                (needs-edge . ".github/workflows/ci.yml: fast-env now declares the explicit single-element edge needs: [lint] — nothing heavier; the fast-env job starts after the lightweight check-name lint gate only")
                (no-ordering-edge . "lint-quality keeps no needs: at all and fast-env does not list lint-quality, so there is no ordering edge between fast-env and lint-quality in either direction — the two jobs run concurrently; tests/test-w9-ci-workflow-verification.rkt pins fast-env's exact needs line, lint-quality's edgelessness, and the checkpoint's fast-env_to_lint-quality_ordering_edge == none")
                (downstream-edges-unchanged . "test keeps needs: [lint, fast-env], test-platform keeps needs: lint, and the aggregate keeps needs: [test, test-platform] — exactly as pinned in W0/W1; tests/test-ci-runtime-contract.rkt (35/35 green) re-pins every live edge against the checkpoint")
                (byte-identical-proof . "the manifest/OS/Racket/lockfile verification steps inside fast-env are untouched; the checkpoint records prepare_action_sha256 be8c614ce36555a0bcbe8671d12699255825109c9ff8c83a8c2a40650a4e5a2d and setup_action_sha256 1a7b517f6c31e537f70dd6139f1b8017b4f0ac632410f38ed27b8e557077521e, and the w9 suite pins that both digests equal the live .github/actions/prepare-racket-environment/action.yml and .github/actions/setup-racket/action.yml bytes — the prepared-environment contract is unchanged")
                (loud-fallback . "the loud fallback survives: the w9 suite pins that the aggregate still hard-fails when fast-env's prepared-env verification fails (needs.fast-env.result guard) and that the fast-env job itself is declared failure_gate fail_lane with on_restore_failure prepare_env_verify_failure in the checkpoint — a bad prepared env still fails the lane, never silently skips")
                (critical-path-proof . "tests/test-ci-runtime-contract.rkt pins the same-SHA before/after pairing in artifacts/ci-topology/v1.00.26-w2/dag-checkpoint.json: under the after topology fast-env starts at 18:23:14, immediately after the lightweight lint completes at 18:23:12, and finishes at 18:27:55 while lint-quality (18:22:29–18:26:51) is still running — versus the before topology where fast-env waited for lint-quality's completion at 18:26:47/18:26:51; time-to-test-start drops because test (0)'s fast-env dependency now begins ~3m33s earlier (all four timing relations pinned: lint-after completes before fast-env-after starts; fast-env-after starts earlier than fast-env-before; the windows of fast-env-after and lint-quality-after overlap in both directions)")
                (checkpoint-honesty . "the timing record is labeled topology checkpoint — not a cohort with measurement_kind derived-shape-projection: it is the W0-measured baseline shape re-derived under the W2 needs-graph at the SAME head SHA (anchor_sha == head_sha, pinned by test), not a fabricated fresh run")))
