             (verification-invariants . "prepared-env verification steps and their SHAs are pinned byte-identical and the loud fallback is re-pinned by test — the scheduling change cannot silently weaken what fast-env proves before tests restore the artifact")
             (timing-honesty . "the before/after DAG checkpoint is a same-SHA topology projection derived from the measured baseline — explicitly labeled topology checkpoint, not a cohort; no new run was fabricated to decorate the resequencing")
             (rollback . "reverting is a one-line needs-edge restore on the same branch; because no protection set or policy set changes in W2, no fail-open or never-reporting window can open at any point before or during the revert")))
